===Etymology===
A {{borrowing|la|Austria|lang=lv|nocap=1}}, a latinized version of {{etyl|gem|lv}} {{term|ostar||eastern|lang=goh}} (< {{etyl|gem-pro|-}} {{recons|austra||eastern|lang=gem-pro}}; [[cf]]. also {{etyl|lv|-}} {{term|austrumi||east|lang=lv}}), in reference to this land being the {{term|Marchia austriaca||eastern borderland|lang=lv}}. The word was adapted to Latvian spelling ({{suffix||ija|lang=lv}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap|lang=lv}}

===Proper noun===
{{lv-proper noun|f|4th}}

# [[Austria]] {{gloss|[[country]] in [[Central Europe]], with [[Viena]] as its [[capital]]}}
#: '''''Austrijas''' karogs'' — the flag of '''Austria'''
#: '''''Austrijas''' teritorija'' — the territory of '''Austrija'''
#: '''''Austrijā''' ir labi attīstīta tirgus ekonomika'' — in '''Austria''' there is a well developed market economy

